section: compiler
synopsis: ``-fsplit-sections`` is no longer disabled by ``-dynamic``
description:
  ``-dynamic`` used to unset ``-fsplit-sections``, but only when
  ``-fsplit-sections`` appeared earlier on the command line, so the flag meant
  different things depending on the order of the two. Both orders now split
  sections, as do the dynamic outputs of ``-dynamic-too``.

  On Darwin, ``-fsplit-sections`` is now always ignored with a warning: Mach-O
  has poor support for split sections and instead offers
  ``.subsections_via_symbols``, which GHC uses where it's able to.

